The attached image shows that Nano-11 significantly enhances antigen-specific antibody responses *in vivo*, demonstrating its efficacy as a vaccine adjuvant. Anti-recombinant protective antigen (rPA) IgG titers were markedly higher in mice immunized with rPA combined with Nano-11 (at various doses) or aluminum hydroxide (AH) compared to rPA alone. Nano-11 induced antibody levels comparable to AH, with particularly strong responses observed even at its lowest dose tested, indicating a potent immunopotentiating effect for inducing Th2-biased immune responses.